-- title:
--   Special fibre is covered by the two component generic points
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackage p`, that is, the bundle of data and axioms for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` $=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel` of the full modular function field in level $p$ with its coordinate `IgusaScheme.jFull p` over $\mathbb{Z}$: properness, flatness and integrality of the structure morphism `DRModel.toBase p` to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, integral closedness of the sections over affine opens, curve models over $\mathbb{Q}$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identified with the corresponding base changes together with Galois- and place-compatibility, two sections `εinf`, `εzero` over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, a distinguished smooth locus, and the remaining components, among them the curve `𝔛.ratModel κ` and the two morphisms `𝔛.compInf κ`, `𝔛.compZero κ` from it into the base change of `DRModel p` to $\kappa$. Let $O$ be a commutative local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $toκ \colon O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $y$ be a point of the fibre product $\mathfrak{X}_O =$ `DRModel p` $\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}} \operatorname{Spec} O$ whose image under the second projection does not lie in the basic open set $D(p) \subseteq \operatorname{Spec} O$, i.e. $y$ lies in the fibre over $p$. Then $y$ is a specialisation of at least one of the two points obtained by applying `𝔛.compInf κ`, respectively `𝔛.compZero κ`, followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` (the map of pullbacks induced by the identity on `DRModel p` and by $\operatorname{Spec}(toκ)$), to the generic point of the integral scheme $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\ \kappa).C$.
--
--   This is the statement that the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model over a local ring with maximal ideal $(p)$ is the union of the closures of the images of the two generic points of the $\kappa$-fibre, the supersingular-free components indexed by the two cusps; distinctness of the two points is not asserted. It feeds the analysis of the local structure of the special fibre, being used for instance by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.eq_or_eq_baseChangeMap_genericPoint_of_ringKrullDim_stalk_le_one`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.eq_or_eq_baseChangeMap_genericPoint_of_ringKrullDim_stalk_le_one), [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart) and [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.isClosed_or_eq_generic_of_snd_eq_closedPoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.isClosed_or_eq_generic_of_snd_eq_closedPoint).
